<Base title="Our editorial code" description="The rules Honest Penny follows so that money never decides what we recommend: no paid placement, marked links, sources and corrections.">
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Our editorial code</h1>
    <p>These rules apply to every page and every email. If we ever break one, tell us at the <a href="/corrections/">corrections page</a>.</p>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>No paid placement.</strong> No company can pay to appear, to be ranked higher, or to be reviewed.</li>
      <li><strong>We'll say when doing nothing is best.</strong> If no deal beats what you have, we'll say so, even if that means we earn nothing.</li>
      <li><strong>Paid links are always marked.</strong> If we ever earn money when you use a link, it carries an asterisk (*), and we say so on the page. Where we can, we also give a link that pays us nothing.</li>
      <li><strong>Money people don't touch the words.</strong> Anyone who handles commercial deals for us has no say over what a guide recommends.</li>
      <li><strong>Every fact has a source and a date.</strong> We use official sources first (Government of Canada, CRA, Government of Alberta, your city, regulators) and show the date we last checked.</li>
      <li><strong>No invented people.</strong> We never make up authors, experts, quotes or reviews. A person on our team signs off every guide.</li>
      <li><strong>We fix mistakes in the open.</strong> Corrections are made quickly and noted on the page.</li>
      <li><strong>We don't sell your data.</strong> Your email is used to send you our email, and nothing else. See <a href="/privacy/">privacy</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>General information, not personal advice.</strong> We explain options and rules. For decisions about your own situation, we'll tell you who can give free, qualified help.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="muted">Last updated November 24, 2026.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
